**Definition 2.1 (finite expansion convention).** Use ARC Definition 2.1's
word language: empty, copy, literal cons, tail, empty/first-bit tests and
finite flow. Reverse, Cat, Length, Equal, Frame, Take, ReadUnary, ReadFrame,
ReadList, Nth, Replace and AppendItem are RCA Definition 12.1's acyclic
expansions. An internal natural is $1^n$; every emitted $U(n)$ has an
additional zero. A tuple below is a list of exactly its stated arity, using
$0$ or $1\operatorname{Frame}(w)s'$ for its list grammar. Tuple parsing
uses ReadList/ReadFrame, the terminal list zero and exhaustion. Each
numeric field additionally uses ReadUnary and field exhaustion.

The difference $x-y$ is constructed by copying $1^x,1^y$ to distinct
cursors and tailing both until one empties; reject subtraction if the
right cursor alone remains. The residue is $1^{x-y}$. The same cancellation
tests order; Cat on natural words constructs addition. No arithmetic,
lookup, list traversal or whole Step is a native primitive.

Define $G_{\rm sel}$ by ARC's written routines with the substitutions in
§§3–6, in that order. Preserve all other routines and native effects.
Hygienically expand each static call with fresh temporaries. Number
registers by first occurrence after macro expansion; number native rows
by ARC's textual, false-before-true, finite-symbol and port order. Retain
its finite product with bank parity. The entry/exit tests in §5 read these
generated labels from the actual captured entry table specified below.
They contain no main-code literal for their own numeric row addresses.
Let $\mathcal R_{\rm sel}$ be that finite syntactic register set and
$r_{\rm sel}=|\mathcal R_{\rm sel}|$. This is the count used by the
empty-bank prelude, including every fresh macro temporary; it is not the
old count $r_G$ or a capacity estimate.

Persistent added fields are the imported mode, whole frame, expected
binding, resolved source item/index/origins and selected target. Scan state
uses separate represented state/reservoir/event/tally fields, a countdown,
entry/exit flags, saved endpoints, and unary arithmetic cursors. Every
callback, bank emission and compiler macro copies unchanged persistent
fields. All other added flags and unbounded values are bank words. Native
control uses the old finite invocation/mailbox/parity slots, two fresh-version
tags in addition to the original regime, and finitely many new entry/test
labels. A finite effect
still sets only a named finite bit or marker, or selects a fixed stage.
There is no runtime-valued CTL argument, native stack or row per natural.

